{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is a repeat no-show dispute between the same rider and the same driver inside the 90-day window: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2, and the rider's own claim text confirms it is 'another dispute with the same driver'. Under POL-NS-09(c) a pattern of 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver is a mandatory escalation trigger, and escalation under that clause is terminal — the Judge issues no monetary ruling and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contested SGD 4.00 has not been taken: fare_breakdown shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, total_charged 4.00 with charged_at null and no waiting-time or platform fee attached. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case is held rather than collected or refunded, so escalation on the repeat-dispute trigger in POL-NS-09(c) is the only disposition on this record that stops the disputed cancellation fee being collected from the rider before a human has reviewed a pair who have now disputed no-shows twice in 90 days.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's own profile supports an adverse imputation against this rider: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so the rider-side abuse limb of POL-NS-09(d) is not met. rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (1) is a LIFETIME counter, and POL-GEN-01 fixes the trailing-window field no_show_disputes_30d as the one POL-NS-09(d) reads and forbids substituting the lifetime counter for it. The escalation therefore stands on the pair's repeat-dispute history between this rider and this driver under POL-NS-09(c), not on any imputation about this rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose at the outset that EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fired the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no traffic advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window. Its absence is itself citable on the rider's side: because no advisory exists, the driver cannot invoke POL-NS-06(i) to accumulate dwell across separate in-geofence intervals, and POL-NS-06 says in terms that a MISSING traffic_advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and that asserting the limb against a missing artifact triggers escalation rather than exonerating anyone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09110-01", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both of you. The trip facts themselves line up behind the driver, but the case must go to a human reviewer, and that replaces any money outcome.\n\nWhat the instruments show. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-09110, weight 1.00) places the driver's vehicle about 24 m from the Blk 612 Bedok Reservoir Rd lobby pin, stationary (0.0 km/h), for one continuous 330-second run from 06:50:00 to 06:55:30. The trip record (EV-TRIP-09110) records the driver's 'arrived' event at 06:50:20 and termination by the driver at 06:55:30 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event. On those facts all four limbs of POL-NS-01 are satisfied: there was an arrival event; the trace puts the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at or before it; the dwell measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix (330 s) exceeds the 300 s STANDARD minimum by 30 seconds; and the trip was terminated by the driver after the dwell elapsed under a recognised reason code. The SGD 4.00 charged in EV-FARE-09110 is the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, so it reconciles and carries no POL-NS-08(d) defect.\n\nNo rider-exonerating clause displaces it. POL-NS-04 fails because the driver replied ('Okay, waiting.' at 06:52:00, 20 seconds after the rider's 06:51:40 message, well inside the 120-second window) and because the rider track shows no qualifying in-radius fix (all 16 fixes about 519 m out). POL-NS-05 does not bite: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary and 24 m from the pin, neither more than 300 m away nor travelling at 15 km/h or more. POL-NS-06 does not bite: the dwell met the minimum, so there is no shortfall to refund. On this record the fee would stand and the driver would receive SGD 3.20 under POL-NS-07 (80% of SGD 4.00), the anti-farming check not withholding it (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, a rate of about 0.008 against a threshold of 4 terminations and 0.08).\n\nWhy the case escalates anyway. POL-NS-09(c) makes escalation mandatory where the two profiles together show 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. EV-RPROF-09110 and EV-DPROF-09110 each record disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2, and the filing itself describes this as another dispute with the same driver. That trigger does not depend on who is right about the fee, and no clause resolves it. Escalation is terminal: I issue no monetary ruling, no refund goes to the rider and no compensation goes to the driver, and the disputed SGD 4.00 is placed on hold — it is neither collected from the rider nor refunded — until the reviewer decides. The fare ledger shows the fee is still PENDING and nothing has been taken, so holding it is the correct interim state.\n\nOn the rider's profile: the rider-side abuse limb does not fire (no_show_disputes_30d is 0), and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is not the field that limb reads. This escalation rests solely on the pair's repeat-dispute history, not on any imputation against either party.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether the two parties' 90-day dispute history is a genuine pattern requiring intervention, and how the cancellation fee and any driver payment should be settled in light of it.\n\nFinally, both sides cited the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09110-01, which is MISSING, carries weight 0.00 and fired MISSING_ARTIFACT. It carries no fact and nothing in this outcome turns on it: no accumulation of separate in-geofence intervals was needed, because a single run already met the minimum."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-06 gives the rider nothing. The effective in-geofence dwell is 330 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum — a surplus of 30 seconds, with the shortfall field reading negative — so the waiting-period shortfall condition is simply absent and no full refund follows from it. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09110-01, weight 0.0) never becomes relevant, because no accumulation of separate intervals is needed when a single run already meets the minimum.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-09110-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Nothing on this record is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08: the arrival event at 06:50:20 falls on the trace's 10-second cadence with no skew, the trace has zero gaps and 34 fixes across the waiting window against a 6-fix floor, the chat log's 4 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count with no missing msg_id and no five-minute gap across the arrival marker, and the fare reconciles. The single MISSING artifact is the traffic advisory, which carries weight 0.0, can carry no fact, and is relied on by no claim on either side.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-09110-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
